.TH basename "" "Command"
.SH NAME
basename \- strip file name
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbasename \fIfile \fB[\fIsuffix\fB]\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
basename -- strip file name
Usage:	basename file [ suffix ]
.HE
.B basename
strips
.I file
of any leading directory prefix (everything up to and including the
last
.BR / ).
If the optional
.I suffix
argument is given and the result ends with it,
.B basename
strips that too.
.B basename
prints the result on the standard output.
.PP
For example, the command
.DS
	basename /usr/fred/source.c
.DE
prints
.DS
	source.c
.DE
and the command
.DS
	basename /usr/fred/source.c .c
.DE
prints
.DS
	source
.DE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.B sh
